This adds the /spec-report skill, then runs it on its own spec. The
report is the last patch.

The skill reads a spec, judges the working copy against it using
implementation and documentation, uses history and notes only as
context, and commits a sibling report. The report gives a summary
status, conflicts and whether a "conflict plan:" heading covers each,
plans that can be removed, gaps marked ready or not ready to
implement, and what is done, with evidence for every claim but the
status. A sclr report.org beside a lore.org is moved to
sclr-report.org first.

The report was produced by invoking /spec-report as a command, so it
also shows the skill is installed and runs. It finds every
requirement implemented, no conflicts, and nothing left to plan.

One small point for the spec: spec.org:23 lists REPORT--<name>.org as
an example, but the rule at spec.org:25 turns SPEC--<name>.md into
REPORT--<name>.md. The skill follows the rule.

The first two patches are yours from b/dev, "claude: Permit work
based on b/dev" and "claude/skills/spec-report: Initial spec". They
are included so the series applies to trunk in context, as CLAUDE.md
now asks for work based on b/dev.

Changes in v3:
- Include the two b/dev prerequisites in the series.
- Rebase onto the revised spec: SKILL.md now finds conflict plans
  as headings whose text begins with "conflict plan:", and names
  spec files with <name> rather than a glob.
- Regenerate the report by running the skill as a command; it no
  longer raises questions, since the revised spec answers them.
- Link to v2: id:cover.1791830201.git.claude@p7x.dev

